course: dictionary
lesson: 9833
title: Birds that click in the dark
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A swiftlet is a small bird from the swift family. It lives in warm places in Asia and Australia, and many swiftlets nest in caves.
explain: Caves are very dark, so swiftlets cannot find their way by sight. Instead they click and listen for the echoes that bounce back. This is called echolocation. «Some cave swiftlets of Asia click to find their way in pitch-black caves.»
explain: Context helps here. «Cave swiftlets are among the very few birds that echolocate» tells you that echolocation is rare among birds, so the word is worth remembering.
fact: A swiftlet is a small bird of the swift family.
fact: Echolocation means finding your way by making sounds and listening to the echoes that come back.
fact: «Cave swiftlets are among the very few birds that echolocate.»
fact: Some swiftlets build nests from their own hardened spit, and people collect these nests to make bird's nest soup.
fact: Bats also click and listen to echoes, just like some swiftlets.
exercise: What is a swiftlet? | A type of cave rock | A large fish that lives in rivers | A kind of tropical tree | *A small bird of the swift family
exercise: «Some cave swiftlets of Asia click to find their way in pitch-black caves.» What is the name for finding your way by clicking and listening to echoes? | *Echolocation | Migration | Camouflage | Hibernation
exercise: Find and copy the place name in «Some cave swiftlets of Asia click to find their way in pitch-black caves.» | caves | swiftlets | click | *Asia
test: Where do many swiftlets nest? | In deserts | Under the sea | On the ground in fields | *In caves
test: Why do cave swiftlets click in the dark? | *To find their way by listening to the echoes | To scare away fish | To keep themselves warm | To sing to attract a mate
exam: Why are swiftlet nests so costly to collect? | They are made of gold | They fall from the sky | They are sold only in summer | *They must be collected carefully from cave walls so the birds can still breed
